starttime (bin/pidly:136) takes awk's $22 of /proc/PID/stat. The second
field is the process name in parentheses and may contain spaces, which
shifts every later field, so liveness checks misjudge that process without
any error. Strip up to the last ")" and count from there.


Done 2026-11-04: starttime strips through the last ") " and takes field 20 of the rest. tests/identity.sh runs a copy of sleep named "a) b c" and checks the recorded value is the real start time; the old code recorded num_threads (1) for it.
